# tests/mpx4-udp's run list for its `none-user` way (px47, P5 U7): the
# `none` way's lines (user/mpx4-udp-none.run) AS A USER, each under
# px39's `as 1000 1000`, on a machine with no network device, then a
# port below 1024 refused to the user (px45: EACCES, Linux's rule with
# net.ipv4.ip_unprivileged_port_start 1024): 7, and 1023, the highest.
# The Linux side is the same list in a throwaway container with no
# network (tools/linux-tree --runlist), as the same user.
/bin/as 1000 1000 /bin/sockerr
/bin/as 1000 1000 /bin/udploop
/bin/as 1000 1000 /bin/udpfill
/bin/as 1000 1000 /bin/udpecho 7 127.0.0.1 4999
/bin/as 1000 1000 /bin/udpecho 1023 127.0.0.1 4999
